have either (set <symbol> <expr>), which would work as you'd expect
or
(set (<symbol>+) <expr>) where expr may return a sequence (list or vector), or return a sequence
and if that happens we set the elements of (<symbol>+) to the elements of that sequence in order
if sequence exceeds we bind the last symbol to the sequence's tail of unassigned values
if the symbols exceed then we bind all the symbols we don't have values for to nil